            {
                "entry_id": "9a38fc3b-8f4b-3f92-8ac7-62afb91e7bd0",
                "word": "Dalmatic",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c6f43961-78c0-4c53-a76c-b8c3fe36e350",
                        "entry_id": "9a38fc3b-8f4b-3f92-8ac7-62afb91e7bd0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Dalmatic"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e2572ed4-a520-46ac-a2a1-b82a7355fe15",
                        "entry_id": "9a38fc3b-8f4b-3f92-8ac7-62afb91e7bd0",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Dalmatic"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a2be4270-20aa-325a-85e4-b38973a4a29c",
                        "entry_id": "9a38fc3b-8f4b-3f92-8ac7-62afb91e7bd0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Related to Dalmatia and its language and culture; Dalmatian."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9e53de7-179c-49d0-9dd0-981d77fbd3c5",
                                "sense_id": "a2be4270-20aa-325a-85e4-b38973a4a29c",
                                "text": "Jerome translated the Scripture into the Dalmatic tongue, as these men do testify, Alphonsus a Castro, Eckius, Hosius, Erasmus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e690968e-aae5-423d-90b3-fcc1806fb1e7",
                                "sense_id": "a2be4270-20aa-325a-85e4-b38973a4a29c",
                                "text": "In contrast to the situation in Solvenia, where many geographical terms of Latin or Greek origin have entered the Slovenian language through German mediation (ex. cisterna, kanal, katarakt, ocean, sifon, terme itd.), the Dalmatic language has played the role of intermediary in Croatia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b868a62-b14b-47eb-8735-787b0a30ff42",
                                "sense_id": "a2be4270-20aa-325a-85e4-b38973a4a29c",
                                "text": "Croatian language stands out among the remaining South Slavic languages in significant lexical influence received from Romance languages (substrate traces of the Dalmatic language, e.g., jarbol, tunj). Italian significantly influenced the coastal regions of Croatia (especially the parts formerly under Venetian control), while German and, to an extent, Hungarian influenced the continental part."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "eca5949e-154e-3f4c-ba12-dd5a407d589f",
                "word": "dalmatic",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4b83cf37-97c7-4746-acc0-53edb502c778",
                        "entry_id": "eca5949e-154e-3f4c-ba12-dd5a407d589f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dalmatics"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe0fa47c-d02d-3f1b-8aca-c3fd8efe4303",
                        "entry_id": "eca5949e-154e-3f4c-ba12-dd5a407d589f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A long wide-sleeved tunic, which serves as a liturgical vestment in the Roman Catholic and Anglican Churches and is worn by a deacon at the Eucharist or Mass and, although infrequently, by bishops as an undergarment above the alb."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7445ff45-7ca1-49cc-a6da-d26e221eba96",
                                "sense_id": "fe0fa47c-d02d-3f1b-8aca-c3fd8efe4303",
                                "text": "He had [...] dalmatics of white satin and pink silk damask, decorated with tulips and dolphins and fleurs-de-lis [...]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "12ae3bcf-da9e-416a-818b-0b37a76a33c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "eca5949e-154e-3f4c-ba12-dd5a407d589f",
                        "source_sense_id": "fe0fa47c-d02d-3f1b-8aca-c3fd8efe4303",
                        "source_sense_description": "ecclesiastical garment",
                        "target_lang_word": "dalmatique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dalmatique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12f2bda8-df1d-3e83-aa03-2ed658b7a45b",
                                        "entry_id": "af777966-9463-3984-a45e-7c505b0f48ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de tunique qui se fabriquait d’abord en Dalmatie, portée sur leur aube dans certains offices par les diacres et les sous-diacres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Liturgie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c13d3dd-45d4-4ac0-bedd-ef458175d4d3",
                                                "sense_id": "12f2bda8-df1d-3e83-aa03-2ed658b7a45b",
                                                "text": "[…] des frères de charité avec leurs dalmatiques rouges, dont l’un portait une bannière et l’autre la lourde croix d’argent, riaient en dessous, s’amusaient à se bourrer le dos de coups de poing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efaf308f-1ff0-45e7-8815-dd929d09e5bd",
                                                "sense_id": "12f2bda8-df1d-3e83-aa03-2ed658b7a45b",
                                                "text": "La prêtresse de ce sanctuaire, où les orfrois des vieilles dalmatiques luisaient sous le reflet mauve des vitraux, venait d’avoir vingt-cinq ans, petite et mince, d’une beauté brune adorable ; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7807e53-039e-421a-850c-331f4355e462",
                                                "sense_id": "12f2bda8-df1d-3e83-aa03-2ed658b7a45b",
                                                "text": "Faut-il vous rappeler maintenant que la liturgie assigne à tous les vêtements, à tous les ornements de l’Église, un sens différent, selon leur usage et selon leur forme ?\nC’est ainsi, par exemple, que le surplis et l’aube signalent l’innocence […] la dalmatique : la justice dont nous devons faire preuve dans notre ministère […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22820c73-61f1-4cd2-83a9-faf039bf6da4",
                                                "sense_id": "12f2bda8-df1d-3e83-aa03-2ed658b7a45b",
                                                "text": "Il y aura bientôt Michel âgé de sept ans, fragile et léger, à qui il suffirait de jeter sur les épaules une dalmatique pour en faire un ange de Fouquet ou de Roger de la Pasture, mais les yeux ont déjà un arrière-fond de tristesse : on sait à sept ans ce que c’est que la vie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "993ea9c8-7c01-357d-a359-409ee11a1653",
                                        "entry_id": "af777966-9463-3984-a45e-7c505b0f48ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ornement de soie que portent les évêques à l’autel sous leur chasuble."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Liturgie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9aa2e65-4d1e-3e00-a97d-19a8b91ecdc5",
                                        "entry_id": "af777966-9463-3984-a45e-7c505b0f48ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Riche tunique à manches amples et courtes des empereurs romains, de certains souverains et grands personnages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
